@startuml
title Jardinero — block view\nGREY = external service

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor White
skinparam NoteBorderColor Black
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor LightBlue
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor Moccasin
  BackgroundColor<<external>> LightGray
  BorderColor Black
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor Moccasin
  BorderColor Black
}

package "External" as EXT {
  component "Discord" as DiscordX <<external>>
  component "GitHub" as GitHubX <<external>>
  component "Linear" as LinearX <<external>>
}

package "Transport + Adapters" as ADP {
  component "Discord\nadapter" as DA
  component "GitHub\ndelivery" as GA
  component "Linear\ndelivery" as LA
  component "Admin web page\ndashboard" as OA
  component "Scheduler\ncron + polling" as SCH
}

package "Orchestrator" as CORE {
  component "\nEngineCommands\n" as EC
  component "State machines\n\nRequestRouter\nLinearImplementer\nFixImplementer\nPrMaintainer\nLogReviewer\n\nevents.ts -> engine.ts -> state-handlers.ts" as MC
  database "Store\nSQLite" as ST
}

package "Execution" as EXE {
  component "SandboxPool\n\ncaps, kill\nrun lifecycle" as SP
  component "WorkerRunner\nTenki | Mock" as RUN
  component "Tenki\nsandbox + Codex" as TenkiX <<external>>
}

DiscordX --> DA
GitHubX --> GA
LinearX --> LA
DA --> EC : request
GA --> EC : pull request event
LA --> EC : issue event
OA --> EC : operator\ncommand
SCH --> EC : scan / poll / periodic check

EC --> MC : entry point
MC --> ST : instance state + event log

MC --> SP : start sandbox run
SP --> RUN : execute
RUN --> TenkiX : sandbox + Codex
SP --> MC : run succeeded / failed

MC --> ADP : reports

note bottom of MC
  The only place that decides what happens next. An entry point takes
  the instance under a lock and switches on its state; the engine then
  loops the handlers until the instance stops moving.
end note

note bottom of ST
  State lives on the instance of each machine. A sandbox run records
  one execution and points at its instance, which is what makes
  "everything that happened here" answerable.
end note

note bottom of SP
  Executes and rations. Never decides what comes next.
end note

note bottom of RUN
  Two classes of write to the world: the orchestrator reports
  deterministically (Linear activity and issue state, mark PR ready,
  comment reaction), and the agent writes from inside the sandbox
  (push, open PR, reply threads).
end note
@enduml
